#X text 245 108 The general idea behind this multi core approach is
to pass pd~-brds to a new PD subprocess on startup and then pass all
possible methods of input into the pd~ object as messages. Open pd~-brds
to see the modifcations to the parameters. Actions that should be taken
are removing -\$1 from the end of all parameters (this is not a hard
and fast rule but should be applied to all knob parameters.);
